{
  "id": "secondary-auditory-cortex",
  "term": "secondary auditory cortex",
  "definition": "Secondary auditory cortex is a higher-level auditory brain area, often called A2, that works beyond primary auditory cortex (A1). In the source packet, it is described as functioning in a supramodal and multimodal way to support spoken language, and in early congenital deafness it may become functionally uncoupled from A1.",
